WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.163
Docker on your

00:00:00.975 --> 00:00:02.307
Mac with memory

00:00:02.119 --> 00:00:02.991
handed back

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:04.712
Katamaran is an

00:00:04.536 --> 00:00:05.644
open-source way to

00:00:05.456 --> 00:00:06.847
run Docker containers

00:00:06.659 --> 00:00:08.014
and Linux machines

00:00:07.826 --> 00:00:08.946
on Apple silicon

00:00:08.758 --> 00:00:09.300
Macs

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:10.573
all inside one

00:00:10.385 --> 00:00:11.505
virtual machine

00:00:12.022 --> 00:00:12.729
It pairs a

00:00:12.541 --> 00:00:14.392
custom Hypervisor framework

00:00:14.204 --> 00:00:15.465
monitor based on

00:00:15.277 --> 00:00:16.161
libkrun with a

00:00:15.972 --> 00:00:17.234
native Swift app

00:00:17.211 --> 00:00:17.918
and the kat

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:18.826
command-line tool

00:00:19.358 --> 00:00:20.631
File sharing uses

00:00:20.443 --> 00:00:21.940
direct hypercalls and

00:00:21.752 --> 00:00:23.096
unused guest memory

00:00:23.014 --> 00:00:23.791
goes back to

00:00:23.603 --> 00:00:25.360
macOS in sixty-four

00:00:25.172 --> 00:00:26.327
kilobyte blocks

00:00:26.862 --> 00:00:27.876
Full story on

00:00:27.687 --> 00:00:28.583
the dashboard
